{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && cat > update-16.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Final increment for this window. The narrowed precondition of the snapshot-boundary loop says the practical trigger is a snapshot taken while the applied index lags the log end by at least TrailingLogs. I tried to execute that variant (small TrailingLogs plus an auto-snapshotting leader behind a deliberately slow FSM, with a wide uncommitted suffix on the peer) but the local attempt never reached its precondition - the leader's own snapshot was not observed inside the harness window - so it is recorded as an unresolved necessary gap rather than shipped as an experiment that would fail. The three-case experiment already registered and executed stands unchanged.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-compact16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 216, \\\"end_line\\\": 262, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-takesnap16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 72, \\\"end_line\\\": 130, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@q-practical-trigger\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Does the snapshot-boundary loop also occur with a non-zero TrailingLogs when the leader snapshots while its applied index lags the log end by at least TrailingLogs, i.e. is the narrowed precondition reachable through a threshold-triggered snapshot under a real write backlog?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact16\\\", \\\"src-takesnap16\\\"],\n      \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Taking a snapshot at index L while the log end is at least TrailingLogs ahead of L makes compactLogsWithTrailing delete up to L, so the leader's retained log begins above L and the rejoining peer's stale entry at L cannot be reconciled except by repeated whole-snapshot transfers - the same cycle the TrailingLogs=0 witnesses show, but reached with a normal trailing configuration under backlog.\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Run the sealed-partition history with a small TrailingLogs and a leader that snapshots on its own while the FSM lags: the loop is supported if the peer's Restore count grows with its applied index pinned at the auto-snapshot index, and refuted if the peer converges to the leader's applied index with zero installs.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"gaps\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-practical-trigger\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Which concrete harness produces a threshold-triggered snapshot whose index lags the log end by at least TrailingLogs, and does the peer then stay unrepairable? A local attempt with a 15 ms-per-apply FSM, SnapshotThreshold=5, SnapshotInterval=10 ms and TrailingLogs=2 failed to observe any leader snapshot inside its window, so the harness needs to establish the backlog explicitly (for example by driving many client applies faster than the FSM drains them, or by taking the snapshot while a known backlog exists) before any loop claim can be made for a non-zero trailing configuration.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-practical-trigger\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact16\\\", \\\"src-takesnap16\\\"],\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No measurement is claimed. The source arithmetic recorded in the revised Behavior (0b99111e65eb4d9faae97028d6140ff5-knowledge-0, revision 2) says the boundary is compacted away only when lastLogIdx - trailingLogs >= snapshotIndex at the moment of the snapshot, and the measured three-case receipt (CheckRun 0b99df9ed72e4cd2b653c5741e4eec3d) confirms the converse for snapshots taken while the log end only marginally exceeds the snapshot index. What remains untested is the positive direction with TrailingLogs > 0: no execution yet shows a threshold-triggered snapshot under a genuine backlog producing the loop. The local attempt described in the gap is recorded as a failed harness, not as evidence: its precondition check (waiting for the leader's own snapshot index to become non-zero) never fired, so no event described a snapshot at all and nothing about the loop can be inferred from it. The asserted results therefore stay scoped exactly as before - TrailingLogs=0 with a snapshot taken at the log end (single-peer witness CheckRun 7772ad1b5b154d498a27a79806bb0ea7; sealed-partition witness CheckRun f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30; cause isolated by CheckRun beca431464bf44ab9c3354145c21899f) - and the practical-trigger question is left open for a harness that establishes the backlog deliberately.\\\",\n+      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n+        \\\"The failed local attempt produced no observation, so it neither supports nor refutes the positive direction; it only shows that the chosen way of creating a backlog was inadequate.\\\",\n+        \\\"Because the only measured trailing values that looped are 0, the finding must keep that value explicit in its scope until the backlog variant is executed.\\\"\n+      ],\n+      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n+        \\\"No controller receipt exists for this investigation; the local attempt is construction feedback only and is reported as a failed harness.\\\",\n+        \\\"The proposed harness direction (drive applies faster than the FSM drains, or snapshot during a known backlog) was not built to completion, so the achievable backlog depth and the resulting snapshot index were not measured.\\\",\n+        \\\"Everything in this run's snapshot-boundary line remains in-process, five-node, with in-memory transports and stores.\\\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-16.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
